    docs: document DuckBrain auth resolution in VERBS.md conventions (DOC-003)
    
    The conventions block in docs/VERBS.md said nothing about authentication,
    while AUG-039 proved a fresh-box user dies on the first command with no
    documented way out. Add one bullet covering, verified against the code:
    
    - DUCKBRAIN_API_KEY wins (auger.py `_token()`, lines 454-468); unset or
      empty falls through to the token files.
    - Token paths in order: ~/.duckbrain/foreman-status.token, then
      ~/.duckbrain/token (TOKEN_PATHS, lines 107-110); first non-empty wins.
    - A fresh boot creates neither file (AUG-039): the install must set the
      env var or write one of the token files itself.
    - The exact refusal line when nothing resolves:
      "no DuckBrain token: set DUCKBRAIN_API_KEY or ~/.duckbrain/foreman-status.token".
    
    Docs-only change to docs/VERBS.md; no code touched, verb list unchanged.
    ruff check auger.py and python3 -m py_compile auger.py both pass.
---
 docs/VERBS.md | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/VERBS.md b/docs/VERBS.md
index dcf35a0..65d0e11 100644
--- a/docs/VERBS.md
+++ b/docs/VERBS.md
@@ -25,6 +25,14 @@ Conventions every verb shares:
 - A refused write exits non-zero and says why. A model call that fails is fail-closed:
   no verdict is invented, no question is made up, nothing is written on an answer the
   model did not give.
+- Every verb authenticates to DuckBrain the same way: the `DUCKBRAIN_API_KEY` environment
+  variable wins; if it is unset or empty, the token files `~/.duckbrain/foreman-status.token`
+  then `~/.duckbrain/token` are tried in that order and the first non-empty one is used.
+  Nothing creates these files for you — a fresh install does not ship with
+  `~/.duckbrain/foreman-status.token` (AUG-039: on a fresh boot the first command dies),
+  so set the env var or write one of the token files yourself. When nothing resolves,
+  the command exits non-zero with
+  `no DuckBrain token: set DUCKBRAIN_API_KEY or ~/.duckbrain/foreman-status.token`.
 
